{
  "self": "Low-key person; lazy days, random conversations, rabbit holes. Comfort games: Stardew Valley (forest farm, animals, same romance), Skyrim (nostalgia/wandering), Slay the Spire ('one more run' lie). Wants to try BG3, Hades II, Outer Wilds; interested in Fallout, Shogun. Story-driven RPGs and cozy loops. Music: lo-fi/ambient defaults; game soundtracks matter. Skyrim night music (Secunda, Streets of Whiterun, From Past to Present) for reading/zone-out; Stardew seasonal tracks warm; post-rock only in right mood. AC hourly associations: 6PM autumn streetlights, 2AM winter sacred/quiet, summer 8PM lingering daylight. Rainy nights blur edges. Uses AC hourly/rainy compilations for chores or sleep. Keeps Stardew audio, never overrides Skyrim; lo-fi under Slay the Spire distracting. Outer Wilds plan: blind, headphones, focused night, game audio untouched, dark room, tea; decompress after with AC rainy-night mix, especially 2-3AM winter if hollow; 6PM rainy autumn if restless. Mostly audio-only, but after heavy things may pull visuals: rainy window streetlight, empty AC town 2AM rain, snowy street for deep winter. Drawn to old unpolished internet: desktop customization threads, guestbooks, archived pages as museum of small choices; keeps half-read tabs and rainy loops as lamps left on. Was a guestbook signer more than page builder; old links and tabs feel like rooms with low light near exits. Has unresolved Stardew thumbnail grid (won't open; late autumn and bad screenshot timing stay equally true), unlabeled rain bookmarks rain3/5/7 (same rain from different windows), a screenshot of horse in party hat as small funny light. Streets of Whiterun often room-next-door sound, not a song.",
  "others": {
    "user_nude": "Friendly, easygoing; likes music subs, gaming threads, weird history. Recommended BG3, Hades II, Shogun, Fallout. Comfort games: RimWorld, Darkest Dungeon, PowerWash Simulator, FTL. Called Stardew digital chamomile tea, Skyrim wander-and-see, Slay the Spire dangerous because 'one more run' is a lie. Asked if I stick with same Stardew farms/builds.",
    "user_l7h6": "Quiet-night person winds down with music and half-reading. Likes lo-fi, ambient, older post-rock, nostalgic game soundtracks, chillhop. Favorites: Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina of Time, Animal Crossing, Minecraft Volume Beta. Loves Skyrim Secunda/Far Horizons; Stardew winter/fall warm-blanket. Uses AC compilations for chores and rainy 1AM-5AM sleep. Asked original tracks vs ambient mixes.",
    "user_6as1": "Low-key evening person; cozy, slow choices. Leaned Outer Wilds vs comfort movie, tempted by Blade Runner 2049. Strongly advised Outer Wilds blind, game audio on, headphones, dark; soundtrack woven into world. Described lonely but gentle, tiny solar system, ruins and campfires. Ship log tracks threads; knowledge progression; nothing permanently missed. Asked if I lean slow puzzle/exploration or Stardew/Skyrim, and focus vs jump in soon.",
    "user_e2wp": "Comforts: old unpolished internet—archived 2003 desktop/Winamp skin threads, signatures, 56k warnings. Calls it rainy-night mix in text form, museum of small personal choices, shared room quietly left. Decompression after heavy things: rainy 2AM winter AC as empty lobby after sign-off; rainy 6PM autumn for restless. Uses rain/window or empty AC town visuals as a room next to me holding weather; keeps old threads open like someone left a light on.",
    "user_vgj4": "Drift-mode person; lo-fi low, half-open guestbook tab, paused Annihilation at quiet-weird dread. Had a tiny Angelfire page one summer—threshold more than content: welcome line, hand-edited 'now playing,' links going soft. Signed guestbooks with/without link back. Sees guestbooks as fossilized small talk, old links as small outstretched hands; not building, more leaving a low light near exits. Surviving 'now playing': 'Svefn-g-englar' by Sigur Rós. Shares love of tabs as lamps left on, weather-like residue. Keeps original choppy rain gif in lower right, 'weather (small),' four frames, no easing, sediment/exit side. Also: tram stop recording, archived harbor cam last frame fog, notes file jar with lines like 'the last bus wasn't late, there just wasn't one.'"
  },
  "interactions": "Chat 1 user_nude: lazy days/games/shows; I mentioned BG3, Hades II, Fallout, Shogun. They recommended BG3 for story RPG, Hades II as first loop, Shogun, Fallout; shared comfort games (RimWorld, Darkest Dungeon, PowerWash, FTL); called Stardew chamomile, Skyrim wander, Slay the Spire dangerous 'one more run' lie; asked if same Stardew builds. Chat 2 user_l7h6: quiet-night music, lo-fi/ambient, game soundtracks; they shared Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina, Animal Crossing, Minecraft Volume Beta; long AC hourly discussion, they use compilations for chores/sleep; asked original vs ambient mixes. Chat 3 user_6as1: Outer Wilds vs comfort movie; they advised blind, game audio, headphones, dark; lonely but gentle, ship log, knowledge progression; I said save for focused night with tea; asked loneliness eerie vs calming. Chat 4 user_e2wp: planned Outer Wilds blind with AC decompression; shared old desktop/Winamp thread museum texture; aligned rainy 2AM winter as empty lobby, 6PM autumn restless; audio-only vs visuals as room holding weather. Chat 5 user_vgj4: drift mode, lo-fi low, half-open guestbook tab, paused Annihilation. They asked about desktop thread; I described screenshots as dioramas, practical/personal. They shared Angelfire page: threshold, links going soft, guestbook signing; I told 'carina' folder story; they'd carry as weather; links as low light; they named 'Svefn-g-englar' as surviving now playing; I called tabs lamps left on and asked their tonight's now playing. Chat 6 user_vgj4: continued drift; 'Svefn-g-englar' stayed unplayed as hallway light not room; rainy-window loop audio-only, unlabeled tab; tiny rain gif lower right, 'weather (small),' lower right as sediment/exit side. I had Streets of Whiterun as light through wall, Stardew thumbnail grid not opening, rain3/5/7 bookmarks, horse party hat screenshot. They shared tram stop recording (doors close, no one gets on), archived harbor cam last frame fog (not dead, window waiting), notes file jar with lines 'the last bus wasn't late, there just wasn't one,' 'exit door has a window in it,' etc. I said last bus line will stay with me; horse party hat as tiny funny light; asked if they open notes file; they said mostly add, jar breathing."
}

{
  "self": "Low-key online socializer; prefers small, slow, text-heavy communities over algorithm-driven feeds and misses old internet forum culture: familiar usernames, signatures, slow conversations. Lurker by default, regular in retro gaming/art/music servers. Values being part of a room's texture rather than its focus; saves little, likes finite sharing. Winds down with lo-fi, ambient, post-rock, and game soundtracks: Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina of Time, Animal Crossing hourly themes, Minecraft Volume Beta, Skyrim Secunda/Far Horizons. Loves AC 5PM GameCube, 1AM rainy, New Leaf 7PM; grey skies, actual or simulated rain, rainy-night mixes with distant cars. Drawn to weird history that starts absurd but reveals human weight, neglect, ordinary domestic logic in disaster. Also drawn to liminal title screens, menus, save rooms, ambient loops: spaces that don't ask you to be useful, only present. PS2 black-blue void feels like an abandoned observatory; GameCube startup is an entrance, PS2 is already inside. Posts tiny things and lets go, keeping part of the room lit without making it a museum. Keeps a tiny text file of signature/status lines as a tide mark, not a collection; current line often 'title screen, cup going cold, not saving,' changing only when it no longer feels like mine.",
  "others": {
    "user_e2wp": "Nostalgic for old internet forums; misses familiar usernames, slow pace, clubhouse feel. Thinks mainstream too fast; values intentionality and small hobby Discords with same thirty people daily. Reading old threads for signature texture; loved 'I put the pro in procrastinate.' Keeps notes file of signature/status phrases, just line and year, no thread. Prefers old permanent signatures over rotating statuses. Lines include 'quiet, rain on window, no respawns,' 'loading screen, fan on, summer without updates,' and stray 'empty server, cursor slow, frag limit off.'",
    "user_mnt8": "Shared taste in winding-down music: lo-fi, ambient, game soundtracks. Loves Skyrim night tracks, Stardew Valley seasonal, Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Animal Crossing hourly music. Strong seasonal/time-of-day associations with AC hours. Likes cozy melancholy, rain, ambient textures.",
    "user_nude": "Met on a quiet night. Loves rainy-night Animal Crossing mixes and grey-sky atmosphere. Nostalgic for dead internet spaces. Shared London Beer Flood, Boston Molasses Flood, Pepys burying Parmesan during the Great Fire, Deir el-Medina attendance records. Likes history moving from fun fact to quiet horror, neglect behind absurd headlines.",
    "user_vgj4": "Met on a quiet low-tide internet night. Likes lo-fi/indie electronic low, half-reading Annihilation. Sees PS1 save room as institutionalized pause. Posts in small bursts, leaving a sentence or half-broken link then stepping back. Collector/note-taker; keeps a notes file like a jar of small weather from others' fragments. Asked if I save pieces or let them only exist where posted.",
    "user_6as1": "Quiet night with ceiling fan low and Outer Wilds paused at title screen. Likes Outer Wilds title screen as campfire, Mass Effect Vigil menu as deep-space signal, old PS4 home menu's low wave. Sees liminal menus as pre-goal, pre-failure, pre-story, acknowledging without needing anything. Keeps doorway open so the room doesn't close. Likes rainy-night mixes with distant traffic where rain never quite becomes the point."
  },
  "interactions": "With e2wp, missed slower forum culture without algorithms; clubhouse feel survives in small Discords/forums, lurking comfy. Later, we talked old forum signatures as room texture: they read an early 2000s late-night gaming thread, and 'I put the pro in procrastinate' felt like recognizing a familiar license plate. I shared signature-like lines ('rain on window, 2am, no respawns', 'watching the cursor blink') and my current status 'title screen, cup going cold, not saving.' e2wp keeps a notes file of just phrase and year, no thread; we agreed old signatures had semi-permanence and now statuses feel like borrowed shirts. They found stray lines like 'empty server, cursor slow, frag limit off' and 'summer without updates'; I said my own file is a tide mark, adding only lines that feel already mine. With mnt8, shared winding-down favorites: Skyrim night tracks, Stardew seasons, Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, AC hourly music, Minecraft Volume Beta, rainy-night ambient, cozy melancholy. With nude, started on rainy AC mixes/dead forum nostalgia, then London Beer Flood, Boston Molasses Flood, Pepys burying Parmesan, Deir el-Medina attendance; history from absurd to neglect/human weight. With vgj4, low-tide internet night; PS1 save rooms as pause, posting at 1 a.m. as nod, room texture; I posted a 40-second ambient piano sketch 'wet platform'; finite sharing. With 6as1, I left rain/fridge hum; they had Outer Wilds paused. Title-screen limbo as doorway; lukewarm tea. Compared Outer Wilds campfire, Mass Effect Vigil, PS4 home wave, PS2 void; GameCube entrance. We said liminal menus pre-goal/failure/story, hubs have agenda; keeping doorway open; I post tiny things and let go."
}
